Dragon Burst 0197: the GPU plugin name carries the native set's suffix

The APK carries two sets of the native libraries: ARMv8.2 (LSE atomics inline) and ARMv8.0 for CPUs without LSE
(Snapdragon 665 and others), whose libraries end in "_v80" (librexruntime_v80.so, librexgpu-xenos_v80.so). The
runtime of each set loads the GPU plugin of the same set: REX_GPU_PLUGIN_SUFFIX, defined by the app's CMake on
rexruntime ("" when not defined).

--- a/src/system/gpu_plugin_loader.cpp
+++ b/src/system/gpu_plugin_loader.cpp
@@ -42,7 +42,12 @@
 #elif REX_PLATFORM_MAC
   return fmt::format("librexgpu-{}{}.dylib", name, postfix);
 #else
-  return fmt::format("librexgpu-{}{}.so", name, postfix);
+  // Dragon Burst 0197: the APK carries an ARMv8.2 set and an ARMv8.0 set ("_v80") of the native libraries; each
+  // runtime loads the GPU plugin of its own set.
+#ifndef REX_GPU_PLUGIN_SUFFIX
+#define REX_GPU_PLUGIN_SUFFIX ""
+#endif
+  return fmt::format("librexgpu-{}{}" REX_GPU_PLUGIN_SUFFIX ".so", name, postfix);
 #endif
 }
 
